    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Inertia depends strictly on the mass of an object; higher mass means higher inertia.",
        "Recoil velocity of a gun and rocket propulsion are direct applications of the Law of Conservation of Momentum.",
        "Limiting friction is the maximum value of static friction and is always slightly greater than kinetic friction.",
        "Impulse is defined as Force × Time and is equal to the total change in momentum."
      ],
      "id": "vroe9c9"
